\caption(Component count, numerical rank and a selected compression dimension describe different things.)
\alttext(A scree plot has one hundred percent on the first of three returned axes and zero on the other two. Tables expose the spectrum and the constant feature’s preserved offset and unit divisor.)

> Iris measurements

All 150 rows have four complete numeric flower measurements in centimetres. The four
features enter every fit; Species is withheld and supplies colours only afterwards.
Each species has fifty rows. The full-data fits are descriptive, not held-out estimates
of prediction quality. No species label is used to select axes or a retained dimension.

>> Scaled scores and rotation coefficients describe one metric

This baseline centres and sample-standardizes all four measurements. The score
axes mix them linearly; the spectrum table defines their variance shares and the
loadings table preserves each coefficient. A large coefficient means a geometric
contribution under this scaling convention, not a causal or biological importance.
The species separation visible in the scores does not validate a classifier. Even
uncorrelated component scores can be statistically dependent.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pca_iris_scaled.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  using namespace dm::stats;
  const auto               d = dm::datasets::iris();
  const PCA                fit(d, {"Sepal.Length", "Sepal.Width", "Petal.Length", "Petal.Width"});
  std::vector<std::string> species;
  for (auto i : fit.kept_row_indices())
    species.push_back(d.string_at("Species", i));
  auto scores = fit.plot_scores(species).title("Species colours added after fitting");
  scores.y_limits(-3, 4.5);
  auto scree = fit.plot_scree().title("Sample-standardized training spectrum");
  scree.y_limits(0, 100);
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame prep;
  prep.add_column("feature", fit.feature_names());
  prep.add_column("training_mean_cm", fit.means());
  prep.add_column("training_sample_sd_cm", fit.scales());
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(scores).add(scree).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/pca_iris_scaled.svg");
  std::print(
      "{} flowers; {} retained rows; numerical Gram rank {}.\n\n{}\n\n{}\n\n{}\n",
      d.nrows(),
      fit.observations(),
      fit.numerical_rank(),
      prep.to_md(6),
      fit.spectrum().to_md(9),
      fit.loadings_frame().to_md(6));
}
```
