| 3 | 3.08651063 | 0.071722970 | 0.106639448 | 3.08651063 | 0.076935350 |
| 4 | 0.00000000 | 0.000000000 | 0.000000000 | 0.00000000 | 0.000000000 |


First two components retain 95.813207% (scaled) and 97.768521% (raw) of their respective total energies.
Full-basis standardized residual SSE: 3.455299131e-28.
\image(figures/pca_iris_reconstruction.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Eigenvalue tails explain training loss in one metric; raw and scaled PCA solve different reconstruction problems.)
\alttext(Measured standardized RMS coincides with eigenvalue-tail predictions. Original-centimetre RMS curves compare raw and standardized fits across zero to four retained axes. A table preserves all measured errors and tail sums.)

>> Project thirty new flowers without fitting their centre

A fixed row-index split holds out every fifth observation: 120 training rows and
30 test rows. This deterministic split is not a population sampling study. The training
rows alone determine means, sample scales and axes. Test scores use those same axes;
adding another query to their batch cannot change an individual projection. We compare
one test row alone against its projection in the full test batch. Reconstruction curves
measure all test rows against their actual measurements, with no query-centre fit and
no training-tail equality assumed for the test data. The k=2 error describes this one
representation and split, not classification accuracy or a tuned dimension choice.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pca_iris_frozen.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  using namespace dm::stats;
  const auto               d = dm::datasets::iris();
  std::vector<std::size_t> train_rows, test_rows;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < d.nrows(); ++i)
    (i % 5 == 0 ? test_rows : train_rows).push_back(i);
  const auto train = d.take_rows(train_rows), test = d.take_rows(test_rows);
  const PCA  fit(train, {"Sepal.Length", "Sepal.Width", "Petal.Length", "Petal.Width"});
  const auto projected = fit.transform(test), one = fit.transform(test.head(1));
  for (std::size_t c = 0; c < 4; ++c)
    if (projected(0, c) != one(0, c))
      throw std::runtime_error("query batch changed projection");
  auto scores = fit.plot_scores().title("Training axes and untouched projections");
  scores.legend({"training", "test"}, {{37, 99, 235}, {220, 38, 38}})
      .points(projected.col(0), projected.col(1), "test", {220, 38, 38}, 5)
      .y_limits(-3, 4.5);
  const auto a = fit.reconstruction_curve(train), b = fit.reconstruction_curve(test);
  auto       error = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  error
      .line(
          a.numeric_column("components").values(),
          a.numeric_column("preprocessed_rmse").values(),
          "training",
          {37, 99, 235})
      .line(
          b.numeric_column("components").values(),
          b.numeric_column("preprocessed_rmse").values(),
          "test",
          {220, 38, 38})
      .title("Both samples use the training metric")
      .x_label("retained components")
      .y_label("preprocessed RMS per entry")
      .y_limits(0, 1.4);
  auto table = a;
  table.add_column("test_preprocessed_rmse", b.numeric_column("preprocessed_rmse").values());
  table.add_column("test_original_rmse", b.numeric_column("original_rmse").values());
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame means;
  means.add_column("feature", fit.feature_names());
  means.add_column("fitted_mean", fit.means());
  std::vector<double> test_means;
  for (const auto& f : fit.feature_names()) {
    long double sum = 0;
    for (double v : test.numeric_column(f).values())
      sum += v;
    test_means.push_back(double(sum / test.nrows()));
  }
  means.add_column("test_mean_not_used", test_means);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(scores).add(error).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/pca_iris_frozen.svg");
  std::print(
      "{} training rows; {} test rows. Query singleton/batch projections match "
      "exactly.\n\n{}\n\n{}\n",
      train.nrows(),
      test.nrows(),
      means.to_md(6),
      table.to_md(10));
}
```
